{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Hemolytic, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is unique and shows only very low similarity (92.31%) to Temporin-SHa L:23%, G=F: 15%. Chemical modification: A4 is a D-amino acid. C-terminal amidation. Activity: active against Gram+ S. aureus NCTC 13277 MRSA (MIC 14.34 uM), B. subtilis ATCC 23857 (MIC 6.25 uM), Gram- S.typhi ATCC 14028 (MIC 250 uM), E.coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 125 uM), P.aeruginosa ATCC 10145 (MIC >250 uM), and fungi C. albicans ATCC 36082 (MIC 20 uM). Structure: helical in 20 mM SDS. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 90 uM. Breast cancer cells MCF-7 (IC50 17.9 uM), cervical cancer Hela cells (IC50 >100 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39766603", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2024 Dec 13;13(12):1213. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics13121213. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05183", "source_id": "AP05183", "source_numeric_id": "05183", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05183", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Synthesis of Temporin-SHa Retro Analogs with Lysine Addition/Substitution and Antibiotic Conjugation to Enhance Antibacterial, Antifungal, and Anticancer Activities.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Hemolytic, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is unique and shows only very low similarity (64.29%) to Lausporin-1 L:23%, G=F: 15%. Chemical modification: A10 is D-amino acid; C-terminal amidation. Activity: active against Gram+ S. aureus NCTC 13277 MRSA (MIC 3.12 uM), B. subtilis ATCC 23857 (MIC 1.56 uM), Gram- S. typhi ATCC 14028 (MIC 50 uM), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 50 uM), P.aeruginosa ATCC 10145 (MIC 200 uM), and fungi C. albicans ATCC 36082 (MIC 15.6 uM). Structure: helical in 20 mM SDS. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 13.8 uM; hemolytic. Breast cancer cells MCF-7 (IC50 53 uM), cervical cancer Hela cells (IC50 60 uM). SAR: conjugation of XX with the C-terminal lysine sidechain led to RLFP-1; conjugation of XX with the sidechain of K3 led to RLFP-2;", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39766603", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2024 Dec 13;13(12):1213. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics13121213. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05184", "source_id": "AP05184", "source_numeric_id": "05184", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05184", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Synthesis of Temporin-SHa Retro Analogs with Lysine Addition/Substitution and Antibiotic Conjugation to Enhance Antibacterial, Antifungal, and Anticancer Activities.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is unique and shows only very low similarity (64.29%) to Lausporin-1 L:23%, K=F: 15%. Chemical modification: A10, D-amino acid; C-terminal amidation. Activity: active against Gram+ S. aureus NCTC 13277 MRSA (MIC 50 uM), B. subtilis ATCC 23857 (MIC 12.5 uM), Gram- S. typhi ATCC 14028 (MIC 100 uM), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 50 uM), P.aeruginosa ATCC 10145 (MIC 200 uM), and fungi C. albicans ATCC 36082 (MIC 100 uM). Structure: helical in 20 mM SDS. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 >100 uM (not hemo.lytic at 100 uM). Breast cancer cells MCF-7 (IC50 39.9 uM), cervical cancer Hela cells (IC50 56.9 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39766603", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2024 Dec 13;13(12):1213. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics13121213. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05185", "source_id": "AP05185", "source_numeric_id": "05185", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05185", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Synthesis of Temporin-SHa Retro Analogs with Lysine Addition/Substitution and Antibiotic Conjugation to Enhance Antibacterial, Antifungal, and Anticancer Activities.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
